# Comment generated code

Every function, class, and non-obvious block in code you generate gets a comment that says why it is there, what constraint it respects, and what breaks if it moves.

- Comment the purpose, the hardware or timing limit, and the order dependency.
- Do not restate the next line (`// increment i` above `i++`).
- Keep comments next to the code they explain.

```cpp
// Address of the real USB UART, captured before "#define Serial GwDebug".
// After that rename, Serial.write inside write() would recurse.
static HardwareSerial* gwUsb = &Serial;
```
